.TH SCALES 1.SH NAMEscales \- a practice list of scales and chords.SH SYNOPSIS\fBscales\fR[\-d] [\-a] [\-m] [\-c] [outname].SH DESCRIPTION\fBscales\fRdeals the kinds of scale and chord you choose into a random order andwrites them as a practice list, each entry with a tick box, its keysignature and its spelling:.nf    ___   1 F Major (Ionian)      (1  flat :  Bb)            Spelling:   F G A Bb C D E.fiThe list goes to\fBscales.lst\fRin the current directory, or to\fIoutname\fR.\fRChoose at least one kind; with none it asks what you had in mind..SH OPTIONS.TP 12\fB\-d\fRdiatonic scales -- thirty of them..TP 12\fB\-a\fRaltered scales..TP 12\fB\-m\fRmodes..TP 12\fB\-c\fRchords..TP 12\fB\-h\fRthe usage message..SH NOTESNeeds Microware's\fBcio\fR.\fR